From 451508196e3e1917f8ff1d57dac841287c0d0394 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arc-moe <arc-moe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 08:42:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sycl: the native router has no barrier after its early return
 (DG2 GPU hang)

route<NE> launches an 8x32 block, returns rows 1-7 at once, and then
called a work-group barrier. On Alchemist the barrier waits for every
thread of the work-group, the exited ones included, so the kernel never
finished: i915 reset GPU 0 in the first verify window (STRATA_VERIFY_STEPLOG
named the stage: between stage 16 and resident_plan, i.e. the router).
The values are registers and no local memory is used, so the barrier had
nothing to order. Every other early return before a barrier in the SYCL
kernels was checked: all are uniform over the work-group.
---
 sycl/src/kernels/cuda/native_router.dp.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sycl/src/kernels/cuda/native_router.dp.cpp b/sycl/src/kernels/cuda/native_router.dp.cpp
index ed61cfc..121e34d 100644
--- a/sycl/src/kernels/cuda/native_router.dp.cpp
+++ b/sycl/src/kernels/cuda/native_router.dp.cpp
@@ -82,7 +82,10 @@ __dpct_inline__ void route(const float *__restrict__ logits,
     float values[NE / 32];
 #pragma unroll
     for (int i = 0; i < NE / 32; ++i) values[i] = logits[lane + i * 32];
-    item_ct1.barrier(sycl::access::fence_space::local_space);
+    // arc-moe: no work-group barrier here. Rows 1-7 of the 8x32 block returned above, and on Alchemist (DG2) a
+    // barrier waits for every thread of the work-group, the exited ones included: the kernel never finished and
+    // i915 reset the GPU (the first verify window and every decode token). The values are registers, there is no
+    // local memory to order, so the barrier (dpct's __syncthreads) had nothing to do.
     float maximum = -INFINITY;
 #pragma unroll
     for (int i = 0; i < NE / 32; ++i) maximum = sycl::max(maximum, values[i]);
